1
1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,640
我要说一个可能有争议的观点：别写提示词。
I'm going to say something that might be controversial. Don't write prompts.

2
2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:12,400
我不是让你别和智能体说话。我说的是那个大家伙——放在项目根目录、试图解释一切的巨型指令文件。
I don't mean stop talking to your agent. I mean the big one. The giant instruction file at the root of your project, that tries to explain everything.

3
3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:22,400
想知道为什么，我们来打开地球上最大的代码库之一：Firefox。数千万行代码，C++、Rust、JavaScript、Kotlin。
To see why, let's open one of the largest codebases on earth. Firefox. Tens of millions of lines of code. C++, Rust, JavaScript, Kotlin.

4
4
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:27,200
你可能以为它给智能体的指令会长得吓人。根文件只有 73 行。
You would expect its agent instructions to be enormous. The root file is seventy-three lines.

5
5
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:32,229
而它的第一条规则是什么？几乎不要写注释。嗯，开了个好头。
And the very first rule in it? Almost never add comments. So, we're off to a good start.

6
6
00:00:32,229 --> 00:00:41,509
这是我们大多数人都写过的提示词：一个文件，塞着构建步骤、测试命令、代码风格、架构说明，外加一条关于某个不稳定测试的警告。
Here's a prompt most of us have written. One file. Build steps, test commands, style rules, architecture, and a warning about that one flaky test.

7
7
00:00:41,509 --> 00:00:48,379
每个任务都要为这一整份买单。只是改文档里的一个错别字？智能体照样得读一遍垃圾回收器的原理。
Every task pays for all of it. Fixing a typo in the docs? The agent still reads how the garbage collector works.

8
8
00:00:49,029 --> 00:00:58,789
Firefox 的做法不一样。根文件只放放之四海而皆准的东西。然后它列出五个目录，并说：在这里干活时，打开这里面的那份 AGENTS.md。
Firefox does something different. The root file holds only what is true everywhere. Then it lists five directories, and says: when you work in here, open the agents file that lives in here.

9
9
00:00:58,789 --> 00:01:07,989
JavaScript 引擎有一份，排版有一份，WebRender 有一份。每份也就一百行上下，而且只有走进那个目录时才会被读到。
The JavaScript engine has one. Layout has one. WebRender has one. Each is around a hundred lines or less, and each is only read when you step inside.

10
10
00:01:07,989 --> 00:01:13,659
这和提取函数是同一个动作。指令并没有变短，它只是有了作用域。
It's the same move as extracting a function. The instruction didn't get shorter. It got a scope.

11
11
00:01:13,747 --> 00:01:20,707
再看排版模块那份。一共 31 行，而且大部分在说同一件事：先去读这份文档。
Now look inside the layout one. It's thirty-one lines, and most of them say the same thing. Read this document first.

12
12
00:01:20,707 --> 00:01:31,187
它不解释帧树，它指向解释帧树的那个文件。因为那份文档由改代码的人维护，而提示词里的副本到周五就过期了。
It doesn't explain the frame tree. It points to the file that does. Because that document is maintained by the people who change the code, and a copy inside a prompt would be stale by Friday.

13
13
00:01:31,187 --> 00:01:43,507
JavaScript 引擎那份更进一步：它是一张地图。每个目录一行，按脚本流经引擎的顺序排列：解析器、解释器、编译器、垃圾回收器。
The JavaScript engine's file goes one step further. It is a map. One line per directory, in the order a script flows through the engine. Parser, interpreter, compilers, garbage collector.

14
14
00:01:43,507 --> 00:01:47,267
地图告诉你该往哪看，它不会试图成为疆域本身。
A map tells you where to look. It doesn't try to be the territory.

15
15
00:01:47,267 --> 00:01:54,377
那 Claude 专用的那个文件呢？只有一行：引入 AGENTS.md。所有工具，同一个事实来源。
And the Claude specific file? It is one line. It imports the agents file. One source of truth, for every tool.

16
16
00:01:54,381 --> 00:01:59,581
下一个问题。你没法 grep Firefox。好吧，可以，但你得等。
Next problem. You can't grep Firefox. Well, you can, but you'll wait.

17
17
00:01:59,581 --> 00:02:05,341
你可以为此写上一段话：谨慎搜索，限定路径，保持耐心。
You could write a paragraph about that. Search carefully. Restrict your paths. Be patient.

18
18
00:02:05,341 --> 00:02:13,661
或者，你可以递给智能体一个工具。Firefox 自带一个理解代码的命令行搜索：问它某个定义，它就回答。
Or, you can hand the agent a tool. Firefox ships a command line search that understands the code. Ask it for a definition, and it answers.

19
19
00:02:13,661 --> 00:02:17,021
四条示例命令，替代了一整页的忠告。
Four example commands replace a whole page of advice.

20
20
00:02:17,021 --> 00:02:24,621
这就是提示词里的类型系统。一句话是在请求模型守规矩；一个工具让正确的事变成容易的事。
This is the type system of prompting. A sentence asks the model to behave. A tool makes the right thing the easy thing.

21
21
00:02:24,621 --> 00:02:29,251
紧接着下面还有一句很可爱的话：如果不能很快找到，问一下更好。
And there's a lovely line right below it. If you can't find something quickly, it is better to ask.

22
22
00:02:29,444 --> 00:02:36,964
但有些知识确实很长：排查性能回退、迁移翻译字符串、为评审拆分提交。
But some knowledge really is long. Triaging a performance regression. Migrating translated strings. Splitting a commit for review.

23
23
00:02:36,964 --> 00:02:44,964
Firefox 有 24 个这样的东西，叫做 skill。每个都是一个文件夹，带着自己的说明、脚本和参考资料。
Firefox keeps twenty-four of these, and calls them skills. Each one is a folder, with its own instructions, scripts, and references.

24
24
00:02:44,964 --> 00:02:53,844
诀窍在这里：一开始只加载描述，就一段话。剩下的几百行躺在磁盘上，直到任务真正需要它们。
Here's the trick. Only the description is loaded up front. One paragraph. The other few hundred lines stay on disk, until the task actually needs them.

25
25
00:02:53,844 --> 00:03:03,284
而且团队对代价很坦诚。README 里写着：每条描述都带着常驻成本。如果一个 skill 不是对所有人都有用，它就不该放进代码树。
And the team is honest about the price. Their readme says every description carries an always-on cost. If a skill isn't useful to everyone, it doesn't belong in the tree.

26
26
00:03:03,284 --> 00:03:11,684
于是描述变成了接口。写得好的会说明什么时候用，以及什么时候不用：不是用来跑测试的，请用另一个 skill。
So the description becomes an interface. The good ones say when to use them, and when not to. Not for running tests. Use the other skill.

27
27
00:03:11,684 --> 00:03:17,231
有些甚至声明了自己被允许运行哪些命令。这已经不是提示词了，这是函数签名。
Some even declare which commands they are allowed to run. That's not a prompt anymore. That's a signature.

28
28
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:22,510
还有一层。代码评审时，不该靠谁去记住该用哪份指南。
One more layer. During code review, nobody should have to remember which guidance applies.

29
29
00:03:22,510 --> 00:03:33,710
所以有一个很小的规则配置文件。补丁同时碰了 WebIDL 和 C++ 文件，就加载 Web 标准实现指南；碰了前端代码但不是测试，就加载前端指南。
So there is a small config file of rules. If a patch touches a web interface definition and a C++ file, load the web standards guide. If it touches front end code, but not tests, load the front end guide.

30
30
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:37,338
提示词由 diff 来选择，而不是靠某个人的记性。
The prompt is selected by the diff. Not by somebody's memory.

31
31
00:03:37,339 --> 00:03:41,499
提示词和注释得的是同一种病：没有任何东西检查它们。
Prompts have the same disease as comments. Nothing checks them.

32
32
00:03:41,499 --> 00:03:46,859
指令过期时编译器不会警告你。智能体只会照做，而且信心十足。
The compiler won't warn you when an instruction goes out of date. The agent will just follow it. Confidently.

33
33
00:03:46,859 --> 00:03:54,539
Firefox 为此有一条规则，我很喜欢：引用名字，而不是位置。这段文字会比它描述的代码活得更久。
Firefox has a rule for this, and I love it. Reference a name, not a position. This text outlives the code it describes.

34
34
00:03:54,539 --> 00:04:00,327
所以，不写行号，不写“上面那个函数”。只写名字，以及固定到某个版本的链接。
So, no line numbers. No, the function above. Names, and links that are pinned to a revision.

35
35
00:04:00,327 --> 00:04:03,447
那是不是永远都不该写提示词？当然不是。
So should you never write a prompt? Of course not.

36
36
00:04:03,447 --> 00:04:07,367
把代码没法告诉你的东西写下来：那些坑。
Write down what the code can't tell you. The traps.

37
37
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:14,887
比如这条：默认截图显示的并不是真实的渲染器输出。所以永远不要凭一张截图就断定渲染 bug 修好了。
Like this one. A default screenshot does not show the real renderer output. So never conclude a rendering bug is fixed from a screenshot.

38
38
00:04:14,887 --> 00:04:18,247
或者这条：未经明确批准，绝不提交补丁。
Or this. Never submit a patch without explicit approval.

39
39
00:04:18,247 --> 00:04:22,797
读再多源码，智能体也学不到这些。提示词就是为此而存在的。
No amount of reading the source would teach an agent that. That is what prompts are for.

40
40
00:04:22,803 --> 00:04:29,763
还有一点是我没想到的：这些文件是学习一个大型项目的最佳途径。对智能体如此，对人也一样。
And here is the part I didn't expect. These files are the best way to learn a large project. For agents, and for people.

41
41
00:04:29,763 --> 00:04:39,283
从根目录开始，了解哪些事处处成立。走进一个模块，读它的地图。再扫一遍 skill 的描述，看看这里实际在做哪些工作。
Start at the root, to learn what is true everywhere. Step into a module, and read its map. Then skim the skill descriptions, to see what work actually gets done here.

42
42
00:04:39,283 --> 00:04:42,563
几百行读下来，你就知道每样东西住在哪里。
A few hundred lines, and you know where everything lives.

43
43
00:04:42,563 --> 00:04:51,603
所以在给提示词再加一段之前，换个问题问自己：这东西该住在哪？作用域、指针、工具、skill，还是触发器。
So before you add another paragraph to your prompt, ask a different question. Where should this live? A scope, a pointer, a tool, a skill, or a trigger.

44
44
00:04:51,603 --> 00:04:54,196
别写提示词。去建造它们该在的地方。
Don't write prompts. Build the place they belong.
